<h1>Imagination Listings</h1>

From <I>Tuck's Encyclopedia of Science Fiction and Fantasy</I>:
<p>
<pre>
      This magazine was begun by R. A. Palmer as a companion to <I>Other Worlds</I>,
    but was soon taken over by Hamling. Most issues included a long novel, but
    not many were noteworthy, most being in the interplanetary/space 
    opera/adventure field.
      A very good fan section was run by Mari Wolf, Apr 1951-Apr 1956, and then
    by R. Bloch until the magazine ceased. This was considered a great loss, as 
    it was one of the few departments of its type in the magazines. From June 
    1958 space articles (by Henry Bott) were a feature.
      A companion, <i>Imaginative Tales</i>, began in late 1954, changing its title
    to <i>Space Travel</i> before ceasing in 1958. The title <i>Imagination</i> was
    originally suggested by F. J Ackerman and used for a high-class amateur 
    magazine produced by the Los Angeles Science Fantasy Society for 13 issues 
    (Oct 1937 - 1938).
</pre>
